#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Describes what calibration jobs are and how often they run"
msgstr "Menerangkan apakah kerja penentukuran dan seberapa kerap ia dijalankan"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Monitoring, calibrations, and benchmarking"
msgstr "Pemantauan, penentukuran, dan penanda aras"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Monitoring, calibrations, and benchmarking {#monitoring-calibrations-and-benchmarking}"
msgstr "Pemantauan, penentukuran, dan penanda aras {#monitoring-calibrations-and-benchmarking}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calibrating a quantum computer requires optimizing a plethora of parameters defining the electrical signals that actuate the quantum gates and readout operations. Before a quantum computer is released, its initial calibration process involves thoroughly tuning each parameter to achieve the best possible performance based on benchmarks relevant to the quantum computer's expected workloads. Once a quantum computer has been released, the primary goal is to maintain consistent performance for the lifetime of the device. The optimal values of many of the calibrated parameters remain stable indefinitely, but some vary over time as a result of factors such as changes in the environment of two-level systems (TLS) on the quantum processor chip, changes in the ambient conditions (for example, temperature) in the data center, or instability within the control systems.\n"
msgstr "Menentukur komputer kuantum memerlukan pengoptimuman banyak parameter yang menentukan isyarat elektrik yang menggerakkan operasi gate kuantum dan pembacaan. Sebelum komputer kuantum dikeluarkan, proses penentukuran awalnya melibatkan penalaan menyeluruh setiap parameter untuk mencapai prestasi terbaik berdasarkan penanda aras yang relevan dengan beban kerja yang dijangka bagi komputer kuantum tersebut. Setelah komputer kuantum dikeluarkan, matlamat utama adalah untuk mengekalkan prestasi yang konsisten sepanjang hayat peranti. Nilai optimum bagi banyak parameter yang ditentukur kekal stabil tanpa had masa, tetapi sesetengahnya berubah dari masa ke masa akibat faktor seperti perubahan dalam persekitaran sistem dua aras (TLS) pada cip pemproses kuantum, perubahan keadaan ambien (contohnya, suhu) di pusat data, atau ketidakstabilan dalam sistem kawalan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To ensure consistent performance, IBM&reg; quantum computers are frequently monitored to track parameters that may drift over time, run calibrations when needed, and perform daily benchmarking. This page details three processes — monitoring, calibrating, and benchmarking — that work together to ensure that the IBM fleet of quantum computers remains as stable, predictable, and available to users as possible.\n"
msgstr "Untuk memastikan prestasi yang konsisten, komputer kuantum IBM&reg; dipantau dengan kerap bagi menjejaki parameter yang mungkin menyimpang dari masa ke masa, menjalankan penentukuran apabila diperlukan, dan melaksanakan penanda aras harian. Halaman ini memperincikan tiga proses — pemantauan, penentukuran, dan penanda aras — yang bekerjasama untuk memastikan armada komputer kuantum IBM kekal stabil, boleh diramal, dan tersedia kepada pengguna sebanyak mungkin.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Monitoring {#monitoring}"
msgstr "Pemantauan {#monitoring}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Parameter monitoring {#parameter-monitoring}"
msgstr "Pemantauan parameter {#parameter-monitoring}"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Brief parameter monitoring jobs are executed approximately once an hour, automatically interleaved between user jobs, using the full Qiskit Runtime software stack. The results of these jobs are analyzed to check whether any parameters have begun to deviate from acceptable ranges, ideally catching issues before they become significant enough to affect performance to a noticeable level.\n"
msgid "Brief parameter monitoring jobs are executed approximately once an hour, automatically interleaved between user jobs, using the full IBM Quantum Compute Service software stack. The results of these jobs are analyzed to check whether any parameters have begun to deviate from acceptable ranges, ideally catching issues before they become significant enough to affect performance to a noticeable level.\n"
msgstr "Kerja pemantauan parameter ringkas dilaksanakan kira-kira sekali sejam, diselangi secara automatik antara kerja pengguna, menggunakan tindanan perisian Qiskit Runtime yang penuh. Keputusan kerja-kerja ini dianalisis untuk menyemak sama ada mana-mana parameter telah mula menyimpang daripada julat yang boleh diterima, dengan idealnya mengesan isu sebelum ia menjadi cukup ketara untuk menjejaskan prestasi ke tahap yang ketara.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some of the parameters monitored include the following:\n"
msgstr "Beberapa parameter yang dipantau termasuk yang berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Readout angles, amplitudes, and discriminator threshold, ensuring accurate state discrimination, low leakage and stable operation. This includes the operational parameters of our quantum limited amplifiers.\n"
msgstr "Sudut pembacaan, amplitud, dan ambang diskriminator, memastikan pembezaan keadaan yang tepat, kebocoran rendah dan operasi yang stabil. Ini termasuk parameter operasi amplifier kuantum terhad kami.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Single- and two-qubit gate operations, confirming they behave as expected to maintain correct rotation angles and minimize phase and amplitude errors.\n"
msgstr "Operasi gate qubit tunggal dan dua qubit, mengesahkan ia berkelakuan seperti yang dijangka untuk mengekalkan sudut putaran yang betul dan meminimumkan ralat fasa dan amplitud.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Signatures of TLS activity.\n"
msgstr "Tanda-tanda aktiviti TLS.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the results of these monitoring jobs indicate modest deviations from their expected performance, then appropriate calibration jobs are launched. If severe TLS activity is detected, then the calibration strategy for gates associated with affected qubits might be automatically modified (and could include pausing calibrations) until such TLS activity decreases back to acceptable levels.\n"
msgstr "Jika keputusan kerja pemantauan ini menunjukkan penyelewengan kecil daripada prestasi yang dijangka, maka kerja penentukuran yang sesuai akan dilancarkan. Jika aktiviti TLS yang teruk dikesan, maka strategi penentukuran untuk gate yang berkaitan dengan qubit yang terjejas mungkin diubah secara automatik (dan boleh termasuk menghentikan penentukuran sementara) sehingga aktiviti TLS tersebut berkurangan kembali ke tahap yang boleh diterima.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Holistic monitoring {#holistic-monitoring}"
msgstr "Pemantauan holistik {#holistic-monitoring}"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "In addition to jobs monitoring individual parameters are jobs that monitor the performance of the quantum computer more holistically, such as tests that look at the fidelity of generated Bell states, as well as tests of fractional gates and dynamic circuits on quantum computers that support those features. The goal of these tests, which also run through the full Qiskit Runtime stack interleaved with user jobs, is to efficiently validate the overall behavior of the hardware and software. If these tests detect a significant drop in performance, the quantum computer will automatically pause the job queue until the issue is resolved, ensuring that user jobs won't run until the device is performing as expected again.\n"
msgid "In addition to jobs monitoring individual parameters are jobs that monitor the performance of the quantum computer more holistically, such as tests that look at the fidelity of generated Bell states, as well as tests of fractional gates and dynamic circuits on quantum computers that support those features. The goal of these tests, which also run through the full Quantum Compute stack interleaved with user jobs, is to efficiently validate the overall behavior of the hardware and software. If these tests detect a significant drop in performance, the quantum computer will automatically pause the job queue until the issue is resolved, ensuring that user jobs won't run until the device is performing as expected again.\n"
msgstr "Selain kerja yang memantau parameter individu, terdapat kerja yang memantau prestasi komputer kuantum secara lebih menyeluruh, seperti ujian yang melihat kesetiaan keadaan Bell yang dijana, serta ujian gate pecahan dan litar dinamik pada komputer kuantum yang menyokong ciri-ciri tersebut. Matlamat ujian-ujian ini, yang juga berjalan melalui tindanan Qiskit Runtime penuh diselangi dengan kerja pengguna, adalah untuk mengesahkan tingkah laku keseluruhan perkakasan dan perisian secara cekap. Jika ujian-ujian ini mengesan penurunan prestasi yang ketara, komputer kuantum akan secara automatik menghentikan baris gilir kerja sehingga isu diselesaikan, memastikan kerja pengguna tidak akan berjalan sehingga peranti berfungsi seperti yang dijangka semula.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calibrating {#calibrating}"
msgstr "Penentukuran {#calibrating}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calibrations are triggered whenever monitoring jobs indicate that parameters such as pulse amplitudes or angles have deviated from their ideal values. They run throughout the day in between user jobs, and therefore there is no set time period at which calibrations start and finish. These run only on the qubits/gates for which parameter monitoring has identified specific issues, along with any qubits required to run at the same time according to specific batching rules. On Heron QPUs, the total time spent on calibrations is typically under two hours per day.\n"
msgstr "Penentukuran dicetuskan apabila kerja pemantauan menunjukkan bahawa parameter seperti amplitud atau sudut nadi telah menyimpang daripada nilai idealnya. Ia berjalan sepanjang hari di antara kerja pengguna, dan oleh itu tiada tempoh masa tetap di mana penentukuran bermula dan berakhir. Ini hanya dijalankan pada qubit/gate di mana pemantauan parameter telah mengenal pasti isu tertentu, bersama mana-mana qubit yang perlu dijalankan pada masa yang sama mengikut peraturan pengelompokan tertentu. Pada QPU Heron, jumlah masa yang digunakan untuk penentukuran biasanya kurang daripada dua jam sehari.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Single-qubit operations {#single-qubit-operations}"
msgstr "Operasi qubit tunggal {#single-qubit-operations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These calibrations ensure accurate implementation of the single-qubit gates: sx, x, rx (fractional). We adjust:\n"
msgstr "Penentukuran ini memastikan pelaksanaan tepat gate qubit tunggal: sx, x, rx (pecahan). Kami melaraskan:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qubit frequencies\n"
msgstr "Frekuensi qubit\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pulse amplitudes and phases\n"
msgstr "Amplitud dan fasa nadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These calibrations are batched across the affected qubits and executed concurrently where appropriate, with batching strategies tailored to each calibration type.\n"
msgstr "Penentukuran ini dikelompokkan merentasi qubit yang terjejas dan dilaksanakan secara serentak di mana sesuai, dengan strategi pengelompokan yang disesuaikan dengan setiap jenis penentukuran.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two-qubit operations {#two-qubit-operations}"
msgstr "Operasi dua qubit {#two-qubit-operations}"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "CZ and RZZ gate amplitudes and phases (for Heron and Nighthawk processors)\n"
msgstr "Amplitud dan fasa gate CZ dan RZZ (untuk pemproses Heron dan Nighthawk)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "ECR gate amplitudes and phases (for Eagle processors)\n"
msgstr "Amplitud dan fasa gate ECR (untuk pemproses Eagle)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These calibrations are run in batches of non-nearest-neighbor qubits to minimize crosstalk.\n"
msgstr "Penentukuran ini dijalankan dalam kelompok qubit yang bukan jiran terdekat untuk meminimumkan crosstalk.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Readout {#readout}"
msgstr "Pembacaan {#readout}"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Readout pulse angles\n"
msgstr "Sudut nadi pembacaan\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measurement discrimination parameters\n"
msgstr "Parameter diskriminasi pengukuran\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These calibrations are run simultaneously on qubits that require calibration.\n"
msgstr "Penentukuran ini dijalankan serentak pada qubit yang memerlukan penentukuran.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "How calibrations are scheduled {#how-calibrations-are-scheduled}"
msgstr "Cara penentukuran dijadualkan {#how-calibrations-are-scheduled}"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A calibration job cannot run simultaneously while a job or session is running.\n"
msgstr "Kerja penentukuran tidak boleh berjalan serentak semasa kerja atau sesi sedang berjalan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Therefore, during long sessions, the quantum computer may experience reduced effective stability due to delayed or infrequent recalibration.\n"
msgstr "Oleh itu, semasa sesi yang panjang, komputer kuantum mungkin mengalami kestabilan efektif yang berkurangan disebabkan oleh penentukuran semula yang tertangguh atau jarang.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two jobs submitted at the same time might run under different calibration sets, depending on timing.\n"
msgstr "Dua kerja yang dihantar pada masa yang sama mungkin berjalan di bawah set penentukuran yang berbeza, bergantung pada pemasaan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Benchmarking {#benchmarking}"
msgstr "Penanda aras {#benchmarking}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Daily benchmarking gives a comprehensive view of quantum computer performance and generates the metrics sent to users through Qiskit. They help users choose qubits, optimize compilations, and better anticipate expected circuit performance. You can view reported numbers either programmatically or on the [Compute resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) page (click any QPU to open its detailed information card). Find more details about each metric in the [documentation](/guides/qpu-information).\n"
msgstr "Penanda aras harian memberikan pandangan komprehensif tentang prestasi komputer kuantum dan menjana metrik yang dihantar kepada pengguna melalui Qiskit. Ia membantu pengguna memilih qubit, mengoptimumkan penyusunan, dan menjangka prestasi Circuit yang dijangka dengan lebih baik. Anda boleh melihat nombor yang dilaporkan sama ada secara aturcara atau di halaman [Sumber pengiraan](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) (klik mana-mana QPU untuk membuka kad maklumat terperinci). Cari butiran lanjut tentang setiap metrik dalam [dokumentasi](/guides/qpu-information).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Device drift\">\n"
"The impact of device drift (hardware performance that degrades over time) depends on many factors, such as when calibrations were last run, the specific experiment performed, any TLS activities, and so on. If a particular workload is very sensitive to device parameters' error values, you can perform a real-time device parameter benchmarking by following [this tutorial](/tutorials/real-time-benchmarking-for-qubit-selection) in IBM Quantum Learning.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Hanyutan peranti\">\n"
"Impak hanyutan peranti (prestasi perkakasan yang merosot dari masa ke masa) bergantung pada banyak faktor, seperti masa penentukuran terakhir dijalankan, eksperimen tertentu yang dilakukan, sebarang aktiviti TLS, dan sebagainya. Jika beban kerja tertentu sangat sensitif terhadap nilai ralat parameter peranti, anda boleh melaksanakan penanda aras parameter peranti masa nyata dengan mengikuti [tutorial ini](/tutorials/real-time-benchmarking-for-qubit-selection) dalam IBM Quantum Learning.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

